From 5eb33f187af99e4802ae94d38397dc13bde68ac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:44:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read the target machine name from SMOLVM_MACHINE_NAME

Commands that act on an existing machine and otherwise fall back to
"default" (exec, shell, start, stop, status, resize, sync, monitor,
egress-events, network-test) now take their --name from the
SMOLVM_MACHINE_NAME environment variable when the flag is omitted. An
explicit --name still wins. This lets per-project tooling such as direnv
select the machine without repeating --name on every command.

`machine run` (ephemeral) and the commands that create, delete or
modify a named machine are intentionally left unchanged, so the
variable can never make them act on a machine implicitly.

Enables clap's `env` feature, which adds no new dependencies.

Closes #1385
