+/// Environment variable that supplies the target machine for `--name` on the
+/// commands that act on an existing machine and otherwise fall back to
+/// "default" (exec, shell, start, stop, status, ...). An explicit `--name`
+/// always wins. Lets per-project tooling such as direnv pick the machine.
+const MACHINE_NAME_ENV: &str = "SMOLVM_MACHINE_NAME";
+
 /// Resolve `--allow-cidr`, `--allow-host`, and `--outbound-localhost-only` into a CIDR list,
 /// net flag, and the original hostname list (for DNS filtering).
